        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### 1. How good does the model look the usual way?",
          "",
          "Two models, trained and scored on the same random 80/20 split of the cells:",
          "* **Logistic regression:** land cover of the cell only (scikit-learn, as in the Oracle sample).",
          "* **SLX classifier:** land cover of the cell plus its spatial lag. `column_ids` names the columns that get a lag feature.",
          "",
          "Both see balanced classes during training: SLX oversamples the heat-critical cells (`balance_method='random'`), the logistic regression weights them (`class_weight='balanced'`). Balanced accuracy, the mean of the hit rates for both classes, is the main score, because only a fifth of the cells is heat-critical.",
          "",
          "`use_fit_lag` decides where the lag of a test cell comes from: `True` from its nearest **training** cells, `False` from the **test** cells themselves. In a random split the nearest cells of a test cell are mostly training cells, so `True` is the natural choice."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "interpreter" : "md.low",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<h6 id=\"1-how-good-does-the-model-look-the-usual-way\">1. How good does the model look the usual way?</h6>\n<p>Two models, trained and scored on the same random 80/20 split of the cells:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Logistic regression:</strong> land cover of the cell only (scikit-learn, as in the Oracle sample).</li>\n<li><strong>SLX classifier:</strong> land cover of the cell plus its spatial lag. <code>column_ids</code> names the columns that get a lag feature.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both see balanced classes during training: SLX oversamples the heat-critical cells (<code>balance_method='random'</code>), the logistic regression weights them (<code>class_weight='balanced'</code>). Balanced accuracy, the mean of the hit rates for both classes, is the main score, because only a fifth of the cells is heat-critical.</p>\n<p><code>use_fit_lag</code> decides where the lag of a test cell comes from: <code>True</code> from its nearest <strong>training</strong> cells, <code>False</code> from the <strong>test</strong> cells themselves. In a random split the nearest cells of a test cell are mostly training cells, so <code>True</code> is the natural choice.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : "Train and score both models on a random 80/20 split",
        "hasTitle" : true,
        "message" : [
          "%python",
          "",
          "def score(y_true, y_pred):",
          "    return {'ACCURACY': round(metrics.accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred), 3),",
          "            'BALANCED_ACCURACY': round(metrics.balanced_accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred), 3)}",
          "",
          "",
          "def evaluate(evaluation, test_mask):",
          "    \"\"\"Train both models without the test cells, then score them on the test cells.\"\"\"",
          "    train = model_gdf[~test_mask].reset_index(drop=True)",
          "    test = model_gdf[test_mask].reset_index(drop=True)",
          "    X_test = SpatialDataFrame.from_geodataframe(test[FEATURES + ['geometry']])",
          "",
          "    logreg = LogisticRegression(class_weight='balanced', max_iter=1000, random_state=random_state)",
          "    logreg.fit(train[FEATURES].to_numpy(), train[TARGET].to_numpy())",
          "",
          "    slx = SLXClassifier(spatial_weights_definition=KNNWeightsDefinition(k=K), random_state=random_state,",
          "                        balance_method='random')",
          "    slx.fit(SpatialDataFrame.from_geodataframe(train), TARGET, column_ids=FEATURES)",
          "",
          "    preds = {",
          "        'Logistic regression (cell only)':                logreg.predict(test[FEATURES].to_numpy()),",
          "        'SLX, lag from training cells (use_fit_lag=True)': np.ravel(slx.predict(X_test, use_fit_lag=True)),",
          "        'SLX, lag from test cells (use_fit_lag=False)':    np.ravel(slx.predict(X_test, use_fit_lag=False)),",
          "    }",
          "    rows = [{'EVALUATION': evaluation, 'MODEL': name, 'TEST_CELLS': len(test), **score(test[TARGET], p.astype(int))}",
          "            for name, p in preds.items()]",
          "    return slx, preds, pd.DataFrame(rows)",
          "",
          "",
          "rng = np.random.default_rng(random_state)",
          "random_test = rng.random(len(model_gdf)) < 0.2",
          "slx_random, preds_random, results_random = evaluate('Random 80/20 split', random_test)",
          "print(slx_random.summary)",
          "z.show(results_random)"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "table",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
